 "final_text": "I give up. The theorem as stated is false, so it can't be proved.\n\nIn `WithTop \u211d`, `sSup \u2205 = 0`. Lean confirmed this: `sSup (\u2205 : Set (WithTop \u211d)) = 0` compiles. The empty-set case is the problem. Take `n = 1`, `y = 1`, `A = \u2205` and `B = {1}`.\n\n- **Left side:** `minkowskiSum \u2205 B = \u2205`, so `supportFunction (minkowskiSum \u2205 B) y = sSup \u2205 = 0`.\n- **Right side:** `supportFunction \u2205 y + supportFunction B y = 0 + 1 = 1`.\n\nThese differ (0 \u2260 1), so no proof can exist. The statement would hold if `A` and `B` were assumed nonempty, but the file doesn't assume that. I'm not allowed to change the statement, so I left `/work/cam_0540.lean` unchanged, with the `sorry` still in place.",
